From a0b925b60ca7bbfb3a01c057edf455d497edf6eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:07:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Move the app fully to the cloud: durable storage,
 security, and less polling

Phase 2 - object storage
* storage.py: one interface, two backends (local disk for dev/tests/self-hosting,
  Supabase Storage for the cloud).  Two private buckets: ledger-uploads, ledger-temp.
* images.py: every upload is decoded, validated, EXIF-stripped and re-encoded;
  the extension comes from the detected format (fixes crashes on non-ASCII
  file names such as Persian ones); decompression-bomb guard; results are kept
  under Vercel's 4.5 MB response cap.
* Direct browser-to-storage uploads for large files (static/js/direct-upload.js,
  POST /uploads/sign); the browser first shrinks big photos so most uploads
  stay on the app's own domain.
* importer.py: bounded, validating ZIP import (size/entry/zip-bomb limits,
  coerced fields, whitelisted image references); large exports go through a
  short-lived signed download.
* /uploads/<key> now requires login and is cacheable (immutable random keys).

Phase 3 - authorization and security
* security.py + one central before_request that checks every ID in a URL
  belongs to that URL's campaign (closes the cross-campaign read/write holes
  in maps, drawings, pins, battle and sheets).
* nh3 sanitiser replaces the regex one (stored-XSS via unterminated tags and
  via imported notes); CSRF tokens on every form and fetch; secure cookies;
  security headers and CSP; SECRET_KEY required (>=32 chars) in production;
  DB-backed login/registration throttling; 400 instead of 500 for bad input.
* migrations 0002 (Row Level Security on every table: blocks Supabase's public
  Data API) and 0003 (login_attempts).

Phase 4 - deployment tooling
* /healthz diagnostic, supabase_setup.sql, supabase_storage_setup.sql,
  scripts/live_check.py (end-to-end check of a running site),
  scripts/cleanup_temp.py, rewritten VERCEL_DEPLOY.md.
* api/index.py refuses to start on Vercel without the required variables.

Phase 5 - polling
* static/js/poller.js: pauses while the tab is hidden, backs off when idle,
  snaps back on activity.  The map editor's three timers become ONE request
  (GET .../maps/<id>/sync) instead of ~50 requests a minute.

Tests: 238 (unit, HTTP, real-browser, fuzz, multi-process load), run against
Postgres with a fake Supabase Storage server; no network or secrets needed.
